  "sourceSummary": "Poole Hospital NHS Cervical Spine Neck Exercises p2 number7 Scalene Stretch: sit on chair or bed edge, right hand on left shoulder; tilt head right with shoulder still, then slowly rotate left maintaining right ear toward right shoulder. Hold duration is blank for clinician selection. Document is from childrens physiotherapy; this is a movement illustration, not adult clinical prescription. Chosen12degree tilt and18degree rotation and3second hold are not source prescriptions.",
  "motion": "Seated, right hand resting against front/top of left shoulder, left arm down.0-1second right lateral head tilt12degrees,1-2seconds left yaw18degrees with tilt retained,2-5hold,5-6unturn,6-7untilt,7-8rest. Shoulders, torso, hands and feet fixed. No hand on head or assisted neck pull. Quaternion motion distributed across neck01/02/03/head.",
